        {
          "id": 1687781886,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "If indicated in release note I think it is acceptable ? Packager are expected to follow release note (to enable potential new feature they want).\n\nSince this variable doesn't cause much harm I have only deprecated it. It can be replaced easily (I see only one occurrence).\n\nI would be against using the unprefixed name from CMake in headers (macro visibility haven't boundaries). I don't know if it is common to use ws as library but just in case.\nOthers project choose another name specific to the project https://github.com/llvm/llvm-project/blob/9bd32d78a9c8c51929f200ceefe735dc687ab10d/mlir/include/mlir-c/Support.h#L33-L47 so if you want to drop `ENABLE_STATIC` choose WS_BUILDING_SHARED_LIBRARY macro or other prefixed macro.",
          "author": {
            "id": 3557259,
            "username": "Et7f3",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "elie brami",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
