        {
          "id": 1703056601,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "> You suggest I remove in this version `option(ENBALE_STATIC` and just replace it with `BUILD_SHARED_LIBS`?\n\nCorrect. I haven't done the required git archaeology, but I'm guessing `ENABLE_STATIC` was added while our porting our build system from Autotools (and its `--enable-static` flag) to CMake. We got rid of Autotools a long time ago and CMake's standard equivalent is `BUILD_SHARED_LIBS`, so we should just use that.\n\nAs far as deprecating `ENABLE_STATIC` goes, I'd prefer to just tell people to use `BUILD_SHARED_LIBS` if `ENABLE_STATIC` is present. We're early in the 4.2.x release cycle and the next major release is far enough away that it might make sense to do the following:\n\n- Add a deprecation warning in the release-4.2 branch before the upcoming 4.2.1 release. I can push a MR that does this.\n- Add a deprecation warning in the master branch.\n- Drop `ENABLE_STATIC` support entirely in the master branch.\n- Add an item to the release notes in the master branch.",
          "author": {
            "id": 860017,
            "username": "geraldcombs",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Gerald Combs",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://gitlab.com/uploads/-/system/user/avatar/860017/avatar.png?v=1789689689",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/geraldcombs"
